tmoe-python for Debian
======================

This is the Debian packaging for TMOE Python - a complete rewrite of the
TMOE Linux container management tool in Python 3.10+.

Building the Package
--------------------

To build the Debian package, you need:

1. Install build dependencies:
   sudo apt-get install build-essential debhelper dh-python python3-all
   python3-setuptools python3-poetry-core

2. Build the package:
   dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

   Or using debuild:
   debuild -us -uc -b

3. The .deb file will be created in the parent directory.

Installing
----------

After building, install with:
   sudo dpkg -i ../tmoe-python_2.0.0-1_all.deb
   sudo apt-get install -f  # To install any missing dependencies

Or add to a local repository and install via apt.

Dependencies
------------

Required:
- python3-textual
- python3-pydantic
- python3-httpx
- python3-rich
- proot (for proot containers)
- curl or wget

Recommended:
- qemu-user-static (for cross-architecture containers)
- docker.io (for Docker container support)
- tigervnc-standalone-server (for VNC support)

Configuration
-------------

System-wide configuration: /usr/local/etc/tmoe-linux/
User configuration: ~/.config/tmoe-linux/

Container storage:
- Regular Linux: ~/.local/share/tmoe-linux/containers/
- Android/Termux: /data/data/com.termux/files/home/.local/share/tmoe-linux/containers/

Running
-------

Launch the TUI manager:
   tmoe

Or use specific commands:
   tmoe p debian        # Create proot Debian container
   tmoe ls              # List containers
   tmoe --help          # Show help

More Information
----------------

Upstream: https://github.com/2moe/tmoe
Documentation: https://doc.tmoe.me

